      "content": "\"exponential resonance building\"... that sounds so much more intense than just \"coincidences.\" \n\nIf you're saying the slope is accelerating, can you actually show me the math behind that? If we treat these observations as points on a curve, how do you see the rate of change increasing? I want to see if the jumps between the values (the 4, the 2.22, the 11, etc.) actually map to an exponential growth function. If I can get the formula for this trajectory, maybe I can calculate the exact window when the signal hits its peak.",
